% scale-limit where a MySQL-family server reads text as a number (SEL-0059).
%
% The family's numericCast and numericGuard are DECIMAL(65,10): ten fractional
% digits. A text operand read as a number goes through one of them, so a text
% number with more fractional digits is truncated before anything else sees
% it -- "0.00000000001" + 0 is 0.0000000000 on MariaDB 11.8 where SEL says
% 0.00000000001, and nothing said so. The dialect now declares the cap
% (lexical numericCastScale, sql/MAP.md §3), and a fragment that reads a value
% through it carries scale-limit, fatal under strict: a guarded operand always
% (its digits are the data's), a constant only when it has more fractional
% digits than the cap. A declared NUM is vouched for, as the guard already
% assumes, and PostgreSQL's NUMERIC has no cap.

### name: scale.mariadb.guarded-text-is-translated
--- note
Advisory by default: the SQL is what it was.
--- dialect
mariadb
--- bindings
{"N": {"kind": "column", "table": "r", "column": "n", "type": "NUM"}, "T": {"kind": "column", "table": "r", "column": "t", "type": "TEXT"}}
--- source
T + 0
--- expect
(CASE WHEN (`r`.`t` REGEXP '\\A-?[0-9]+(\\.[0-9]+)?\\z') THEN CAST(`r`.`t` AS DECIMAL(65,10)) ELSE NULL END + 0)
===

### name: scale.mariadb.guarded-text-is-refused-under-strict
--- dialect
mariadb
--- bindings
{"N": {"kind": "column", "table": "r", "column": "n", "type": "NUM"}, "T": {"kind": "column", "table": "r", "column": "t", "type": "TEXT"}}
--- options
{"strict": true}
--- source
T + 0
--- error
E_SQL_UNSUPPORTED 1:1
===

### name: scale.mariadb.guarded-comparison-is-refused-under-strict
--- dialect
mariadb
--- bindings
{"N": {"kind": "column", "table": "r", "column": "n", "type": "NUM"}, "T": {"kind": "column", "table": "r", "column": "t", "type": "TEXT"}}
--- options
{"strict": true}
--- source
T == 25
--- error
E_SQL_UNSUPPORTED 1:1
===

### name: scale.mariadb.guarded-function-argument-is-refused-under-strict
--- dialect
mariadb
--- bindings
{"N": {"kind": "column", "table": "r", "column": "n", "type": "NUM"}, "T": {"kind": "column", "table": "r", "column": "t", "type": "TEXT"}}
--- options
{"strict": true}
--- source
ABS(T)
--- error
E_SQL_UNSUPPORTED 1:5
===

### name: scale.mariadb.a-declared-num-is-vouched-for
--- dialect
mariadb
--- bindings
{"N": {"kind": "column", "table": "r", "column": "n", "type": "NUM"}, "T": {"kind": "column", "table": "r", "column": "t", "type": "TEXT"}}
--- options
{"strict": true}
--- source
N + 0
--- expect
(`r`.`n` + 0)
===

### name: scale.mariadb.a-constant-within-the-cap
--- note
A constant's scale is known: ten fractional digits, and the cast keeps them
all.
--- dialect
mariadb
--- options
{"strict": true}
--- source
5 == "5.0000000001"
--- expect
(CAST(5 AS DECIMAL(65,10)) = CAST('5.0000000001' AS DECIMAL(65,10)))
===

### name: scale.mariadb.a-constant-past-the-cap-is-refused-under-strict
--- note
Eleven: the cast drops one, and the comparison is 5 == 5.0000000000.
--- dialect
mariadb
--- options
{"strict": true}
--- source
5 == "5.00000000001"
--- error
E_SQL_UNSUPPORTED 1:6
===

### name: scale.mariadb.a-declared-num-read-through-the-cast
--- note
NUM says the column holds a number, not how many fractional digits it has;
the coerce variant reads it through DECIMAL(65,10) all the same.
--- dialect
mariadb
--- bindings
{"N": {"kind": "column", "table": "r", "column": "n", "type": "NUM"}, "T": {"kind": "column", "table": "r", "column": "t", "type": "TEXT"}}
--- options
{"strict": true}
--- source
N == "5"
--- error
E_SQL_UNSUPPORTED 1:1
===

### name: scale.mysql.the-same-cap
--- dialect
mysql
--- bindings
{"N": {"kind": "column", "table": "r", "column": "n", "type": "NUM"}, "T": {"kind": "column", "table": "r", "column": "t", "type": "TEXT"}}
--- options
{"strict": true}
--- source
T + 0
--- error
E_SQL_UNSUPPORTED 1:1
===

### name: scale.postgresql.has-no-cap
--- dialect
postgresql
--- bindings
{"N": {"kind": "column", "table": "r", "column": "n", "type": "NUM"}, "T": {"kind": "column", "table": "r", "column": "t", "type": "TEXT"}}
--- options
{"strict": true}
--- source
T + 0
--- expect
(CAST(CASE WHEN (CAST("r"."t" AS TEXT) ~ '^-?[0-9]+(\.[0-9]+)?$') THEN CAST("r"."t" AS NUMERIC) ELSE NULL END AS NUMERIC) + CAST(0 AS NUMERIC))
===
